MNF15-P1-D D2 gate log (2026-11-14) — compressor workspace reuse

D2 mechanism (single shipped workspace, evidence-selected):
  The zstd-3 probe context is owned by the pick's ProbeCache and REUSED
  across misses: per probe `ZSTD_reset_session_only` (the exact directive
  the zio writer itself applies between its concatenated frames) on a
  context whose parameters — compression level 3 + frame checksum — were
  set once at creation; the input then goes through `zio::Writer` +
  `raw::Encoder::with_context(&mut CCtx)` — the SAME driver code the
  fresh path uses, only the context is retained.
  The zlib class measured REUSE-NEUTRAL and is NOT shipped: the D2
  attribution instrument (12800x2 misses, deterministic adversarial
  corpus incl. empty/1 B/repetitive/32-64 KB bodies) measured
  fresh-vs-reused at ~0.99x — flate2's fresh state is a cheap fixed-size
  struct next to the deflate work itself. zlib probes therefore stay on
  the fresh ZlibEncoder path (stateless by construction).
  Per-probe allocations on the shipped path: ONE context + one recycled
  sink buffer, lifetime = pick. Fresh vintage allocated a full CCtx per
  miss.

D2 gate results (all green):
  D2.1 fresh/reused parity   : adversarial sequence (empty, 1 B, random
      97 B/512 B/774 B/2 KB/32 KB, 4096xzero, 8192xA5, gradient-
      patterned, 64 KB zeros, long-jump back-reference, empty-again)
      through ONE workspace per configuration, EVERY length == the fresh
      oracle (p1d_d2_state_isolation_parity — the gate initially FAILED
      on a recycled-sink bug [append instead of clear] and was fixed;
      the parity gate is real, not decorative).
  D2.2 state isolation       : the sequence IS small/large/random/
      repetitive alternation incl. immediate repeats after same-length
      calls (D2.4 folded in).
  D2.3 configuration isolation: both probe configurations through ONE
      cache, interleaved per body in both orders (p1d_d2_config_isolation);
      zlib has no workspace, so no cross-config contamination surface.
  D2.4 reset correctness     : repeated calls, empty bodies at positions
      0 and mid-sequence, back-to-back same-body runs.
  D2.5 candidate identity    : committed 200-candidate manifest reproduced
      byte-exactly.
  D2.6 corpus identity       : 30/30 Maximum + 30/30 Balanced digests
      identical, total 810,816 = the anchor.
  D2.7 external validation   : hubble (wire-decoded round trip) re-encoded
      BYTE-IDENTICAL (1,452,400 B); 363.3 s wall vs D1's 383.2 (-5.2%) —
      with matched evidence, reversing D1's open +1.7% observation: the
      zstd probe mass is what hubble's atlas-heavy pick pays for, and
      workspace reuse is exactly its remedy.
  D2.8 performance attribution:
      zstd-3 probe: reused 1.4 us vs fresh 4.0 us = 2.95x per miss
        (p1d_d2_attribution, 12800x2 misses).
      zlib probe: fresh 43.1 us/probe (reuse-neutral; not shipped).
      Maximum corpus wall (B5): 428.3 (D1) -> 414.5 s = -3.2%
        cumulative 1,127.9 -> 414.5 s = -63.2% (2.72x).
      Balanced corpus wall: 39.87 (D1) -> 28.92 s = -27.4%
        cumulative 165.92 -> 28.92 s = -82.6% (5.74x).
      RSS (B6): corpus peak 108.6 MB (+0.7 over D1's 107.9 — the
        workspace is a fixed context + one recycled buffer).
  D2.9 robustness            : fmt + clippy -D warnings + rustdoc clean;
      release suite 91 tests / 0 failed (incl. the D2 gates); fuzz
      525 trials, 0 panics.
Cache budgets (body 8 MiB + tile 8 MiB), probe configurations, library
versions (zstd 0.13.3 / zstd-safe 7.3.0 / flate2 1.1.10 — zstd-safe now
a direct =-pinned dependency on the already-present crate: NO new code
versions), candidate order and memo hit/miss behavior: all unchanged
(D2 changes only the COST of executing a cache miss — the served cost is
always the true compression length of the same body under the same
configuration).
Wire: untouched. Decoder: untouched.
